    (themselves M3 part 2 P1's richcmp.py's). It finds the workbook part through
    the package relationship; W, the first <sheet> in <sheets> order whose
    relationship type is a worksheet's, and its part; W's root children by byte
    spans, each main one placed by its own copy of the 39-name table of ECMA-376
    Part 1, 18.3.1.99. From the input it builds the W the design gives
    (specs/0025 "The pass", "The calls"):
    
      <sheetPr>      its first main <pageSetUpPr>'s start tag with fitToPage="1"
                     first and every other attribute after it as written, in its
                     order; or, when it has none, <pageSetUpPr fitToPage="1"/>
                     with <sheetPr>'s prefix at the end of its content (no
                     18.3.1.82 child comes after it); every other byte kept, an
                     empty one opened; a <sheetPr> the input lacks created with
                     the root's prefix holding that one child
      <printOptions> its start tag with horizontalCentered="1" first, every
                     other attribute after it as written, in its order
      <pageMargins>  left="0.5" first, the same way; a created one holds the six,
                     Excel's defaults for the five not given (right 0.7, top
                     0.75, bottom 0.75, header 0.3, footer 0.3)
      <pageSetup>    fitToWidth="1" fitToHeight="0" orientation="landscape"
                     first, in ruling 3's order, the same way (its relationship
                     id kept as any other attribute)
      <headerFooter> its start tag kept (an odd text sets no flag), an empty one
                     opened; its main <oddHeader> and <oddFooter> dropped and the
                     sample's two written with its prefix, each before the first
                     main child 18.3.1.46 puts after it, else at the end of the
                     content, in that order, as the crate places them; the texts
                     escaped (&Lemend&R&P of &N, &Cemend)
    
    each element the input lacks created with the root's prefix before the first
    main root child the table puts after it. It compares:
    
      rest_same    W with every main <sheetPr>, <printOptions>, <pageMargins>,
                   <pageSetup> and <headerFooter> cut out is the input's W with
                   its own cut out, byte for byte
      places       the main root children's names are the input's with each
                   created one where the design puts it
      schema_order the main root children are in the table's order, one of each
                   of the five
      pr_rest      <sheetPr> with its first main <pageSetUpPr>'s start tag put
                   back as the input's (or a created one cut out) is the input's
                   (opened when empty), or the created <sheetPr> with nothing in it
      fit_set      that <pageSetUpPr>'s start tag is the design's, byte for byte,
                   and read with ElementTree carries fitToPage 1
      pr_order     read with ElementTree, <sheetPr>'s main children are in
                   18.3.1.82's order (tabColor, outlinePr, pageSetUpPr)
      po_set       <printOptions>'s start tag is the design's, byte for byte (set
                   attribute first, the rest the input's in order), and carries
                   horizontalCentered 1
      pm_set       <pageMargins>'s start tag likewise, left 0.5
      ps_set       <pageSetup>'s start tag likewise, fitToWidth 1, fitToHeight 0,
                   orientation landscape
      rid_same     <pageSetup>'s relationship id attribute (a name ending ":id")
                   is the input's, byte for byte, or absent as in the input
      hf_tag       <headerFooter>'s start tag is the input's (opened when empty),
                   or the created one's with no attribute
      hf_texts     read with ElementTree, <headerFooter> holds one main
                   <oddHeader> and one <oddFooter>, each with no child and the
                   sample's text
      hf_kept      <headerFooter>'s content with its main <oddHeader> and
                   <oddFooter> cut out is the input's with its own cut out
      hf_order     read with ElementTree, <headerFooter>'s main children are in
                   18.3.1.46's order
      w_bytes      W is exactly the W the design gives
      others_same  every entry but W is the input's, byte for byte, the names the
                   input's in the input's order
      read_back    read with ElementTree, one of each of the five, one main
                   <pageSetUpPr> in <sheetPr>
      xml_values   with --diff, the runner's diff.<label>.tsv for the pair: its xml
                   "values" rows are W's alone, and its in_only and out_only are
                   the one-sided counts of the input's W's values against the
                   design's W's, each value keyed as xlsx-diff keys one (an
                   attribute by its element's and its own resolved names and its
                   value; a text node by its element's resolved name and its
                   text; whitespace-only text and namespace declarations not
                   values), counted here with ElementTree (specs/0024 P1
                   verification ruling 6: the expectation is derived); without
                   --diff, no
      flagged      with --diff, the diff's entry row for W carries the flag
                   descriptor exactly when the input's local header sets general
                   purpose bit 3, and no other row is flagged; without --diff, no
    
    It prints ONE line of counts and yes/no flags and no text, reference, sheet
    name or part name. --parts prints W's part name and 1, 0 or - for whether
    the input's entry of that name sets general purpose bit 3, one per line, for
    the log to compare with the runner's rows without printing them. --plant
    <flag> changes the output as read so that the named flag turns to no; the
    line then says planted=yes, or planted=no when the pair gives the plant
    nothing to change.
    """
    import collections
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
    import zipfile
    
    MAIN = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/spreadsheetml/main")
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships")
    
    # ECMA-376 Part 1, 18.3.1.99, the worksheet root's children in order: this
    # program's own copy (specs/0018, "Creating an element"), not the crate's.
    TABLE = (
        "sheetPr dimension sheetViews sheetFormatPr cols sheetData sheetCalcPr "
        "sheetProtection protectedRanges scenarios autoFilter sortState "
        "dataConsolidate customSheetViews mergeCells phoneticPr "
        "conditionalFormatting dataValidations hyperlinks printOptions pageMargins "
        "pageSetup headerFooter rowBreaks colBreaks customProperties cellWatches "
        "ignoredErrors smartTags drawing legacyDrawing legacyDrawingHF drawingHF "
        "picture oleObjects controls webPublishItems tableParts extLst").split()
    assert len(TABLE) == 39
    # 18.3.1.82: <sheetPr>'s children in order; 18.3.1.46: <headerFooter>'s.
    PR_CHILDREN = ("tabColor", "outlinePr", "pageSetUpPr")
    HF_CHILDREN = ("oddHeader", "oddFooter", "evenHeader", "evenFooter", "firstHeader", "firstFooter")
    FIVE = ("sheetPr", "printOptions", "pageMargins", "pageSetup", "headerFooter")
    
    FLAGS = ("rest_same", "places", "schema_order", "pr_rest", "fit_set", "pr_order", "po_set",
             "pm_set", "ps_set", "rid_same", "hf_tag", "hf_texts", "hf_kept", "hf_order", "w_bytes",
             "others_same", "read_back", "xml_values", "flagged")
    
    COMMENT = b"<!-- planted -->"
    # The sample's constants (tools/emend-copy, --pagesetup-sample), in the
    # order ruling 3 writes them.
    FIT_SET = ((b"fitToPage", b"1"),)
    PO_SET = ((b"horizontalCentered", b"1"),)
    PM_SET = ((b"left", b"0.5"),)
    PM_CREATED = ((b"left", b"0.5"), (b"right", b"0.7"), (b"top", b"0.75"), (b"bottom", b"0.75"),
                  (b"header", b"0.3"), (b"footer", b"0.3"))
    PS_SET = ((b"fitToWidth", b"1"), (b"fitToHeight", b"0"), (b"orientation", b"landscape"))
    HEADER = b"&amp;Lemend&amp;R&amp;P of &amp;N"
    FOOTER = b"&amp;Cemend"
    HEADER_TEXT = "&Lemend&R&P of &N"
    FOOTER_TEXT = "&Cemend"
    
    
    def local(tag):
        if tag.startswith("{"):
            ns, _, name = tag[1:].partition("}")
            return ns, name
        return "", tag
    
    
    def rels_name(part):
        d, base = posixpath.split(part)
        return posixpath.join(d, "_rels", base + ".rels") if base else "_rels/.rels"
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        """(Id, Type, resolved target or None) of a part's rels."""
        name = rels_name(part)
        if name not in z.namelist():
            return []
        out = []
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(name)).iter("{%s}Relationship" % RELS):
            external = el.get("TargetMode") == "External"
            target = el.get("Target", "")
            resolved = None if external else (
                target[1:] if target.startswith("/")
                else posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(posixpath.dirname(part), target)))
            out.append((el.get("Id"), el.get("Type", ""), resolved))
        return out
    
    
    def workbook_of(z):
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        return office[0] if len(office) == 1 else None
    
    
    def pick_w(z, workbook):
        """W's part, or None: the first main <sheet> whose relationship is a
        worksheet's."""
        by_id = {i: (ty, t) for (i, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook)}
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(workbook)).iter():
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == "sheet":
                rid = next((el.get("{%s}id" % a) for a in ATTR if el.get("{%s}id" % a)), None)
                ty, target = by_id.get(rid, ("", None))
                if ty in (ATTR[0] + "/worksheet", ATTR[1] + "/worksheet"):
                    return target
        return None
    
    
    TOKEN = re.compile(rb"<!--.*?-->|<!\[CDATA\[.*?\]\]>|<[!?][^>]*>|<(/?)[^>]*?(/?)>", re.S)
    
    
    def top_level(data):
        """One (start, end) span per top-level element of some bytes."""
        spans = []
        depth = 0
        at = 0
        for m in TOKEN.finditer(data):
            tok = m.group(0)
            if tok.startswith(b"<!") or tok.startswith(b"<?"):
                continue
            if m.group(1):
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((at, m.end()))
            elif m.group(2):
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((m.start(), m.end()))
            else:
                if depth == 0:
                    at = m.start()
                depth += 1
        return spans
    
    
    def qname(raw):
        return re.match(rb"<([^\s/>]+)", raw).group(1)
    
    
    def split_name(q):
        p, _, n = q.rpartition(b":")
        return (p + b":" if p else b""), n.decode()
    
    
    def start_tag(raw):
        return raw[:raw.find(b">") + 1]
    
    
    def opened(tag):
        slash = tag.rfind(b"/")
        return tag[:slash] + tag[slash + 1:]
    
    
    ATTRS_RE = re.compile(rb'\s([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')')
    
    
    def attributes(tag):
        """[(name, bytes from the name to the closing quote)] of a start tag, in
        order, namespace declarations among them."""
        return [(m.group(1), tag[m.start(1):m.end()]) for m in ATTRS_RE.finditer(tag)]
    
    
    def root_span(data):
        """(start of the root's start tag, end of it, start of the root's
        content, end of it, the root's prefix)."""
        m = re.search(rb"<([^\s/>?!]+)", data)
        close = data.find(b">", m.start())
        q = m.group(1)
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return m.start(), close + 1, close + 1, close + 1, split_name(q)[0]
        return m.start(), close + 1, close + 1, data.rfind(b"</"), split_name(q)[0]
    
    
    def is_main(raw, parent_prefix, parent_main):
        """Whether an element whose bytes start `raw` is in the main namespace:
        its own declaration of its prefix, else its parent's when the prefix is
        the parent's."""
        p, _ = split_name(qname(raw))
        tag = start_tag(raw)
        decl = rb'\sxmlns:' + re.escape(p[:-1]) if p else rb"\sxmlns"
        own = re.search(decl + rb'\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag)
        if own:
            return own.group(1)[1:-1].decode() in MAIN
        return p == parent_prefix and parent_main
    
    
    def children(data, a, b, rp, parent_main):
        """[(start, end, main local name or None)] of the elements in data[a:b]."""
        out = []
        for (x, y) in top_level(data[a:b]):
            raw = data[a + x:a + y]
            n = split_name(qname(raw))[1]
            out.append((a + x, a + y, n if is_main(raw, rp, parent_main) else None))
        return out
    
    
    def content_span(data, x, y):
        """(start, end) of an element's content, equal for an empty tag."""
        raw = data[x:y]
        tag = start_tag(raw)
        if tag.endswith(b"/>"):
            return x + len(tag), x + len(tag)
        return x + len(tag), x + raw.rfind(b"</")
    
    
    def rels_prefix_of(tag):
        """The prefix a start tag binds to the relationships namespace, or None."""
        for m in re.finditer(rb'\sxmlns:([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag):
            if m.group(2)[1:-1].decode() in ATTR:
                return m.group(1)
        return None
    
    
    def bit3(zin, name):
        """1 or 0 for whether the input's entry sets general purpose bit 3, -
        when there is no such entry."""
        try:
            return "1" if zin.getinfo(name).flag_bits & 0x08 else "0"
        except KeyError:
            return "-"
    
    
    def cut(data, spans):
        """data with the spans cut out."""
        out, at = [], 0
        for (x, y) in sorted(spans):
            out.append(data[at:x])
            at = y
        out.append(data[at:])
        return b"".join(out)
    
    
    def first_insert(kids, after, root_end):
        """The offset before the first main root child the table puts after the
        position `after`, or the root's end."""
        for (x, _, nm) in kids:
            if nm in TABLE and TABLE.index(nm) > after:
                return x
        return root_end
    
    
    def merged(tag, sets):
        """A start tag with `sets` first, in their order, and every other
        attribute after them as written, in its order; empty when it was."""
        names = [n for (n, _) in sets]
        kept = b"".join(b" " + raw for (n, raw) in attributes(tag) if n not in names)
        head = b"".join(b" " + n + b'="' + v + b'"' for (n, v) in sets)
        return b"<" + qname(tag) + head + kept + (b"/>" if tag.endswith(b"/>") else b">")
    
    
    def rid_of(tag):
        """The bytes of a start tag's attribute whose name ends ':id', or None."""
        for (n, raw) in attributes(tag):
            if n.endswith(b":id") and not n.startswith(b"xmlns"):
                return raw
        return None
    
    
    def shape_of(w, root_ns):
        """What the comparison reads of a W: its root's spans and prefix, its root
        children, and the spans of each of the five."""
        ts, te, a, b, rp = root_span(w)
        kids = children(w, a, b, rp, root_ns in MAIN)
        s = {"ts": ts, "te": te, "a": a, "b": b, "rp": rp, "kids": kids}
        for n in FIVE:
            s[n] = [(x, y) for (x, y, nm) in kids if nm == n]
        return s
    
    
    def element_parts(w, span):
        """(start tag, prefix, content start, content end, main children) of an
        element."""
        x, y = span
        raw = w[x:y]
        p = split_name(qname(raw))[0]
        ca, cb = content_span(w, x, y)
        return start_tag(raw), p, ca, cb, children(w, ca, cb, p, True)
    
    
    def whole(tag, content, q):
        """An element of that start tag and content, an empty tag opened."""
        head = opened(tag) if tag.endswith(b"/>") else tag
        return head + content + b"</" + q + b">"
    
    
    def setup_pr_of(w, span):
        """(start, end of its start tag) of the first main <pageSetUpPr> of a
        <sheetPr>, or None."""
        tag, p, ca, cb, kids = element_parts(w, span)
        for (kx, ky, nm) in kids:
            if nm == "pageSetUpPr":
                return kx, kx + len(start_tag(w[kx:ky]))
        return None
    
    
    def hf_design(win, span, rp):
        """The <headerFooter> the design gives."""
        if span is None:
            return (b"<" + rp + b"headerFooter><" + rp + b"oddHeader>" + HEADER + b"</" + rp + b"oddHeader><"
                    + rp + b"oddFooter>" + FOOTER + b"</" + rp + b"oddFooter></" + rp + b"headerFooter>")
        x, y = span
        tag, p, ca, cb, kids = element_parts(win, span)
        # The content as the crate holds it: element children (main, by name)
        # and the bytes between them.
        pieces, at = [], ca
        for (kx, ky, nm) in kids:
            if kx > at:
                pieces.append((None, win[at:kx]))
            pieces.append((nm, win[kx:ky]))
            at = ky
        if cb > at:
            pieces.append((None, win[at:cb]))
        for (name, text) in (("oddHeader", HEADER), ("oddFooter", FOOTER)):
            pieces = [pc for pc in pieces if pc[0] != name]
            rank = HF_CHILDREN.index(name)
            new = (name, b"<" + p + name.encode() + b">" + text + b"</" + p + name.encode() + b">")
            where = next((i for (i, (nm, _)) in enumerate(pieces)
                          if nm in HF_CHILDREN and HF_CHILDREN.index(nm) > rank), len(pieces))
            pieces.insert(where, new)
        return whole(tag, b"".join(raw for (_, raw) in pieces), qname(tag))
    
    
    def design(win, s):
        """The W the design gives for the input, or None when the input is out
        of what the sample can write (two of one of the five)."""
        if any(len(s[n]) > 1 for n in FIVE):
            return None
        rp = s["rp"]
        edits = []  # (start, end, order, bytes)
        # <sheetPr>
        if s["sheetPr"]:
            x, y = s["sheetPr"][0]
            tag, p, ca, cb, kids = element_parts(win, s["sheetPr"][0])
            sp = setup_pr_of(win, s["sheetPr"][0])
            if sp is not None:
                px, pe = sp
                content = win[ca:px] + merged(win[px:pe], FIT_SET) + win[pe:cb]
            else:
                content = win[ca:cb] + b"<" + p + b'pageSetUpPr fitToPage="1"/>'
            edits.append((x, y, 0, whole(tag, content, qname(tag))))
        else:
            at = first_insert(s["kids"], 0, s["b"])
            edits.append((at, at, 0, b"<" + rp + b"sheetPr><" + rp + b'pageSetUpPr fitToPage="1"/></' + rp + b"sheetPr>"))
        for (name, sets, created) in (("printOptions", PO_SET, PO_SET), ("pageMargins", PM_SET, PM_CREATED),
                                      ("pageSetup", PS_SET, PS_SET)):
            idx = TABLE.index(name)
            if s[name]:
                x, y = s[name][0]
                raw = win[x:y]
                tag = start_tag(raw)
                edits.append((x, y, idx, merged(tag, sets) + raw[len(tag):]))
            else:
                at = first_insert(s["kids"], idx, s["b"])
                edits.append((at, at, idx, merged(b"<" + rp + name.encode() + b"/>", created)))
        idx = TABLE.index("headerFooter")
        if s["headerFooter"]:
            x, y = s["headerFooter"][0]
            edits.append((x, y, idx, hf_design(win, s["headerFooter"][0], rp)))
        else:
            at = first_insert(s["kids"], idx, s["b"])
            edits.append((at, at, idx, hf_design(win, None, rp)))
        out, at = [], 0
        for (x, y, _, el) in sorted(edits, key=lambda e: (e[0], e[2])):
            out.append(win[at:x])
            out.append(el)
            at = y
        out.append(win[at:])
        return b"".join(out)
    
    
    def et_first(root, name):
        for el in root:
            ns, nm = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and nm == name:
                return el
        return None
    
    
    def et_count(root, name):
        return sum(1 for el in root if local(el.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(el.tag)[1] == name)
    
    
    def values_of(root):
        """The values of an ElementTree as xlsx-diff keys them: each attribute
        (namespace declarations are not attributes here) by element, attribute
        and value; each text node that is not whitespace alone by its element
        and its text (a node's element is the one it stands in: an element's
        text is its own, its tail its parent's)."""
        vals = collections.Counter()
        ws = " \t\n\r"
    
        def walk(el):
            for (k, v) in el.attrib.items():
                vals[("a", el.tag, k, v)] += 1
            if el.text and el.text.strip(ws):
                vals[("t", el.tag, el.text)] += 1
            for c in el:
                walk(c)
                if c.tail and c.tail.strip(ws):
                    vals[("t", el.tag, c.tail)] += 1
    
        walk(root)
        return vals
    
    
    def plant(flag, wout, others, st):
        """(wout, others) changed so that `flag` turns to no, or None when the
        pair gives the plant nothing to change."""
        s = shape_of(wout, st["root_ns"])
        o = dict(others)
        if any(len(s[n]) != 1 for n in FIVE):
            return None
        prx, pry = s["sheetPr"][0]
        pr_tag, pr_p, pr_ca, pr_cb, pr_kids = element_parts(wout, s["sheetPr"][0])
        sp = setup_pr_of(wout, s["sheetPr"][0])
        hfx, hfy = s["headerFooter"][0]
        hf_tag, hf_p, hf_ca, hf_cb, hf_kids = element_parts(wout, s["headerFooter"][0])
    
        def in_tag(name, old, new):
            x, _ = s[name][0]
            tag = start_tag(wout[x:])
            if old not in tag:
                return None
            return wout[:x] + tag.replace(old, new, 1) + wout[x + len(tag):], o
    
        if flag == "rest_same":
            return wout[:s["te"]] + COMMENT + wout[s["te"]:], o
        if flag == "places":
            # A second copy of the first main root child that is none of the
            # five, right after it: the order stays the table's, the names are
            # one more.
            other = [(x, y) for (x, y, nm) in s["kids"] if nm not in (None,) + FIVE]
            if not other:
                return None
            x, y = other[0]
            return wout[:y] + wout[x:y] + wout[y:], o
        if flag == "schema_order":
            # The <printOptions> moved to the root's end.
            x, y = s["printOptions"][0]
            el = wout[x:y]
            rest = wout[:x] + wout[y:]
            end = rest.rfind(b"</")
            return rest[:end] + el + rest[end:], o
        if flag == "pr_rest":
            end = len(pr_tag) - (2 if pr_tag.endswith(b"/>") else 1)
            new = pr_tag[:end] + b' planted="1"' + pr_tag[end:]
            return wout[:prx] + new + wout[prx + len(pr_tag):], o
        if flag == "fit_set":
            if sp is None:
                return None
            px, pe = sp
            tag = wout[px:pe]
            new = tag.replace(b'fitToPage="1"', b'fitToPage="0"', 1)
            return (wout[:px] + new + wout[pe:], o) if new != tag else None
        if flag == "pr_order":
            return wout[:pr_cb] + b"<" + pr_p + b'tabColor rgb="FF000000"/>' + wout[pr_cb:], o
        if flag == "po_set":
            return in_tag("printOptions", b'horizontalCentered="1"', b'horizontalCentered="0"')
        if flag == "pm_set":
            return in_tag("pageMargins", b'left="0.5"', b'left="0.6"')
        if flag == "ps_set":
            return in_tag("pageSetup", b'orientation="landscape"', b'orientation="portrait"')
        if flag == "rid_same":
            x, _ = s["pageSetup"][0]
            tag = start_tag(wout[x:])
            rid = rid_of(tag)
            if rid is not None:
                new = tag.replace(rid, rid[:-1] + b"x" + rid[-1:], 1)
            else:
                end = len(tag) - (2 if tag.endswith(b"/>") else 1)
                new = (tag[:end] + b' xmlns:pl="' + ATTR[0].encode() + b'" pl:id="rIdPlanted"' + tag[end:])
            return wout[:x] + new + wout[x + len(tag):], o
        if flag == "hf_tag":
            end = len(hf_tag) - (2 if hf_tag.endswith(b"/>") else 1)
            new = hf_tag[:end] + b' planted="1"' + hf_tag[end:]
            return wout[:hfx] + new + wout[hfx + len(hf_tag):], o
        if flag == "hf_texts":
            x, y = s["headerFooter"][0]
            el = wout[x:y]
            new = el.replace(b">" + FOOTER + b"<", b">" + FOOTER + b"x<", 1)
            return (wout[:x] + new + wout[y:], o) if new != el else None
        if flag == "hf_kept":
            return wout[:hf_cb] + b"<" + hf_p + b"evenHeader>x</" + hf_p + b"evenHeader>" + wout[hf_cb:], o
        if flag == "hf_order":
            odd = [(kx, ky) for (kx, ky, nm) in hf_kids if nm == "oddHeader"]
            if not odd:
                return None
            kx, ky = odd[0]
            el = wout[kx:ky]
            rest = wout[:kx] + wout[ky:]
            at = hf_cb - (ky - kx)
            return rest[:at] + el + rest[at:], o
        if flag == "w_bytes":
            return wout + b"\n", o
        if flag == "others_same":
            name = next(iter(o), None)
            if name is None:
                return None
            o[name] = o[name] + COMMENT
            return wout, o
        if flag == "read_back":
            if sp is None:
                return None
            px, pe = sp
            kid = next((wout[kx:ky] for (kx, ky, nm) in pr_kids if kx == px), None)
            if kid is None:
                return None
            end = px + len(kid)
            return wout[:end] + kid + wout[end:], o
        if flag in ("xml_values", "flagged"):
            return wout, o
        raise KeyError(flag)
    
    
    def yn(v):
        return "yes" if v else "no"
    
    
    def main():
        args = sys.argv[1:]
        zin = zipfile.ZipFile(args[0])
        wb = workbook_of(zin)
        if wb is None or wb not in zin.namelist():
            print("error=no-workbook")
            return
        part = pick_w(zin, wb)
        if part is None or part not in zin.namelist():
            print("error=no-worksheet")
            return
        names = zin.namelist()
        win = zin.read(part)
        root_ns = local(ET.fromstring(win).tag)[0]
        if args[1:] == ["--parts"]:
            print(part)
            print(bit3(zin, part))
            return
        zout = zipfile.ZipFile(args[1])
        rest = args[2:]
        diff_path = flag_plant = None
        while rest:
            if rest[0] == "--diff" and len(rest) >= 2:
                diff_path, rest = rest[1], rest[2:]
            elif rest[0] == "--plant" and len(rest) >= 2:
                flag_plant, rest = rest[1], rest[2:]
                if flag_plant not in FLAGS:
                    print("error=unknown-plant")
                    return
            else:
                print("error=usage")
                return
        out_names = zout.namelist()
        wout = zout.read(part) if part in out_names else b""
        others = {nm: zout.read(nm) for nm in out_names if nm != part}
    
        s_in = shape_of(win, root_ns)
        want = design(win, s_in)
        if want is None:
            print("error=out-of-design")
            return
        st = {"root_ns": root_ns}
        planted = False
        if flag_plant is not None:
            changed = plant(flag_plant, wout, others, st)
            if changed is not None:
                wout, others = changed
                planted = True
        extra = flag_plant if planted else None
    
        flags = dict.fromkeys(FLAGS, False)
        s_out = shape_of(wout, root_ns) if wout else None
        created = {n: 0 if s_in[n] else 1 for n in FIVE}
        created_fit = 1 if (not s_in["sheetPr"] or setup_pr_of(win, s_in["sheetPr"][0]) is None) else 0
        rp = s_in["rp"]
        hf_kept_out = -1
        if s_out is not None:
            cut_in = cut(win, [sp for n in FIVE for sp in s_in[n]])
            cut_out = cut(wout, [sp for n in FIVE for sp in s_out[n]])
            flags["rest_same"] = cut_in == cut_out
            want_places = [nm for (_, _, nm) in s_in["kids"] if nm is not None]
            for n in FIVE:
                if created[n]:
                    idx = TABLE.index(n)
                    at = next((i for (i, nm) in enumerate(want_places) if nm in TABLE and TABLE.index(nm) > idx),
                              len(want_places))
                    want_places.insert(at, n)
            locals_out = [nm for (_, _, nm) in s_out["kids"] if nm is not None]
            flags["places"] = locals_out == want_places
            pos = [TABLE.index(nm) for nm in locals_out if nm in TABLE]
            flags["schema_order"] = pos == sorted(pos) and all(locals_out.count(n) == 1 for n in FIVE)
            if len(s_out["sheetPr"]) == 1:
                ox, oy = s_out["sheetPr"][0]
                otag, op, oca, ocb, okids = element_parts(wout, s_out["sheetPr"][0])
                osp = setup_pr_of(wout, s_out["sheetPr"][0])
                if osp is not None:
                    px, pe = osp
                    if s_in["sheetPr"] and not created_fit:
                        isp = setup_pr_of(win, s_in["sheetPr"][0])
                        itag = win[isp[0]:isp[1]]
                        back = wout[ox:px] + itag + wout[pe:oy]
                        flags["fit_set"] = wout[px:pe] == merged(itag, FIT_SET)
                    else:
                        pend = next((ky for (kx, ky, nm) in okids if kx == px), pe)
                        back = wout[ox:px] + wout[pend:oy]
                        flags["fit_set"] = wout[px:pend] == merged(b"<" + op + b"pageSetUpPr/>", FIT_SET)
                    if s_in["sheetPr"]:
                        ix, iy = s_in["sheetPr"][0]
                        itag = start_tag(win[ix:iy])
                        inner = win[ix + len(itag):iy] if not itag.endswith(b"/>") else b"</" + qname(itag) + b">"
                        flags["pr_rest"] = back == (opened(itag) if itag.endswith(b"/>") else itag) + inner
                    else:
                        flags["pr_rest"] = back == b"<" + rp + b"sheetPr></" + rp + b"sheetPr>"
            for (name, sets, made, flag) in (("printOptions", PO_SET, PO_SET, "po_set"),
                                             ("pageMargins", PM_SET, PM_CREATED, "pm_set"),
                                             ("pageSetup", PS_SET, PS_SET, "ps_set")):
                if len(s_out[name]) == 1:
                    ox, oy = s_out[name][0]
                    otag = start_tag(wout[ox:oy])
                    if s_in[name]:
                        itag = start_tag(win[s_in[name][0][0]:s_in[name][0][1]])
                        flags[flag] = otag == merged(itag, sets)
                    else:
                        flags[flag] = otag == merged(b"<" + rp + name.encode() + b"/>", made)
                    if name == "pageSetup":
                        irid = rid_of(start_tag(win[s_in[name][0][0]:])) if s_in[name] else None
                        flags["rid_same"] = rid_of(otag) == irid
            if len(s_out["headerFooter"]) == 1:
                ox, oy = s_out["headerFooter"][0]
                otag, op, oca, ocb, okids = element_parts(wout, s_out["headerFooter"][0])
                odd_o = [(kx, ky) for (kx, ky, nm) in okids if nm in ("oddHeader", "oddFooter")]
                hf_kept_out = sum(1 for (_, _, nm) in okids if nm is not None and nm not in ("oddHeader", "oddFooter"))
                if s_in["headerFooter"]:
                    itag, ip, ica, icb, ikids = element_parts(win, s_in["headerFooter"][0])
                    flags["hf_tag"] = otag == (opened(itag) if itag.endswith(b"/>") else itag)
                    odd_i = [(kx, ky) for (kx, ky, nm) in ikids if nm in ("oddHeader", "oddFooter")]
                    flags["hf_kept"] = (cut(wout[oca:ocb], [(x - oca, y - oca) for (x, y) in odd_o])
                                        == cut(win[ica:icb], [(x - ica, y - ica) for (x, y) in odd_i]))
                else:
                    flags["hf_tag"] = otag == b"<" + rp + b"headerFooter>"
                    flags["hf_kept"] = cut(wout[oca:ocb], [(x - oca, y - oca) for (x, y) in odd_o]) == b""
            flags["w_bytes"] = wout == want
        try:
            root_o = ET.fromstring(wout) if wout else None
        except ET.ParseError:
            root_o = None
        root_i = ET.fromstring(win)
        count_in = {n: et_count(root_i, n) for n in FIVE}
        count_out = {n: -1 for n in FIVE}
        if root_o is not None:
            count_out = {n: et_count(root_o, n) for n in FIVE}
            pr_o = et_first(root_o, "sheetPr")
            setups = [] if pr_o is None else [c for c in pr_o if local(c.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(c.tag)[1] == "pageSetUpPr"]
            if pr_o is not None:
                order = [PR_CHILDREN.index(local(c.tag)[1]) for c in pr_o
                         if local(c.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(c.tag)[1] in PR_CHILDREN]
                flags["pr_order"] = order == sorted(order)
            flags["fit_set"] = flags["fit_set"] and len(setups) >= 1 and setups[0].get("fitToPage") == "1"
            po = et_first(root_o, "printOptions")
            flags["po_set"] = flags["po_set"] and po is not None and po.get("horizontalCentered") == "1"
            pm = et_first(root_o, "pageMargins")
            flags["pm_set"] = flags["pm_set"] and pm is not None and pm.get("left") == "0.5"
            ps = et_first(root_o, "pageSetup")
            flags["ps_set"] = (flags["ps_set"] and ps is not None and ps.get("fitToWidth") == "1"
                               and ps.get("fitToHeight") == "0" and ps.get("orientation") == "landscape")
            hf = et_first(root_o, "headerFooter")
            if hf is not None:
                heads = [c for c in hf if local(c.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(c.tag)[1] == "oddHeader"]
                foots = [c for c in hf if local(c.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(c.tag)[1] == "oddFooter"]
                flags["hf_texts"] = (len(heads) == 1 and len(foots) == 1 and len(list(heads[0])) == 0
                                     and len(list(foots[0])) == 0 and heads[0].text == HEADER_TEXT
                                     and foots[0].text == FOOTER_TEXT)
                order = [HF_CHILDREN.index(local(c.tag)[1]) for c in hf
                         if local(c.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(c.tag)[1] in HF_CHILDREN]
                flags["hf_order"] = order == sorted(order)
            flags["read_back"] = all(count_out[n] == 1 for n in FIVE) and len(setups) == 1
        flags["others_same"] = (list(others) == [nm for nm in names if nm != part]
                                and [nm for nm in out_names] == names
                                and all(others[nm] == zin.read(nm) for nm in others))
    
        # The runner's diff for the pair (specs/0024 P1 verification ruling 6):
        # the xml values row and the descriptor flags against what the rules give.
        in_only = out_only = want_in = want_out = flagged_rows = want_flagged = -1
        side_in = values_of(root_i)
        side_want = values_of(ET.fromstring(want))
        want_in = sum((side_in - side_want).values())
        want_out = sum((side_want - side_in).values())
        if extra == "xml_values":
            want_out += 1
        if diff_path is not None:
            rows = [l.split("\t") for l in open(diff_path, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n") if l]
            values = {c[1]: c for c in rows if len(c) >= 7 and c[0] == "xml" and c[2] == "values"}
            if part in values:
                in_only, out_only = int(values[part][5]), int(values[part][6])
            flags["xml_values"] = (list(values) == [part] and in_only == want_in and out_only == want_out)
            ents = [{"name": c[1], "status": c[2], "flags": c[16]} for c in rows
                    if len(c) == 17 and c[0] == "entry"]
            flagged_rows = sum(1 for r in ents if r["flags"])
            wanted = {part: ("descriptor" if bit3(zin, part) == "1" else "")}
            if extra == "flagged":
                wanted = {nm: ("" if f else "descriptor") for (nm, f) in wanted.items()}
            want_flagged = sum(1 for f in wanted.values() if f)
            flags["flagged"] = (len(ents) > 0 and flagged_rows == want_flagged
                                and all(r["flags"] == wanted.get(r["name"], "") for r in ents))
    
        tag_in = win[s_in["ts"]:s_in["te"]]
        rid_in = 0
        if s_in["pageSetup"]:
            rid_in = 0 if rid_of(start_tag(win[s_in["pageSetup"][0][0]:])) is None else 1
        print(" ".join(
            ["found=1", "planted=%s" % yn(planted)]
            + ["created_%s=%d" % (n, created[n]) for n in FIVE]
            + ["created_fit=%d" % created_fit, "prefixed=%d" % (1 if rp else 0)]
            + ["%s_in=%d" % (n, count_in[n]) for n in FIVE]
            + ["%s_out=%d" % (n, count_out[n]) for n in FIVE]
            + ["rid_in=%d" % rid_in, "hf_kept_out=%d" % hf_kept_out,
               "r_bound_in=%d" % (0 if rels_prefix_of(tag_in) is None else 1),
               "in_only=%d" % in_only, "in_only_want=%d" % want_in,
               "out_only=%d" % out_only, "out_only_want=%d" % want_out,
               "flagged_rows=%d" % flagged_rows, "flagged_want=%d" % want_flagged]
            + ["%s=%s" % (f, yn(flags[f])) for f in FLAGS]))
    
    
    main()
